cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DecodeForge or its retained results, please cite this repository."
title: "DecodeForge: Evidence-backed Q8 kernel compilation for TinyLlama decode"
authors:
  - family-names: Magidin
    given-names: Max
repository-code: "https://github.com/maxmagidin/decodeforge"
url: "https://github.com/maxmagidin/decodeforge"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  DecodeForge is a Rust compiler and guarded PyTorch runtime that lowers typed
  blockwise-Q8 linear operations into deterministic scalar and ARM64 NEON
  kernels, audits native artifacts, and retains reproducible correctness,
  machine-code, and performance evidence for TinyLlama query projections on an
  Apple M4.
